WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.069
So after months and months and months and
months and months, seven months, lawmakers

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:12.620
have finally agreed to a second coronavirus
stimulus and they have not yet voted on it.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.379
They've agreed on it. The House and Senate
still need to vote on it. But in this story,

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:21.630
I'll tell you everything that you might be
getting and also what big business is getting

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:27.340
and what nobody's getting, which is very,
very important. Sadly, this is mostly too

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.531
little, too late. Like, if you want to just
click off and go to a different story. It's

00:00:30.531 --> 00:00:36.050
mostly too little, too late. And you'll see
why momentarily. But let's dig into it. The

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:43.170
package in total is 900 billion dollars. It
will include 600 dollar payments to adults

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:50.949
earning up to 75000 dollars, with the possibility
of an additional 600 per dependent child living

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:56.870
at home. Although the language and the specifics
on that may still change, it's not completely

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:04.539
clear. Restarted enhanced unemployment will
be in place for 300 dollars per week for 11

00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:10.271
weeks. Remember, the original enhanced unemployment
was 600 a week. This will be 300 a week. There

00:01:10.271 --> 00:01:17.579
will be 284 billion dollars for businesses.
The program will be restarted. There will

00:01:17.579 --> 00:01:25.750
be expanded eligibility for nonprofits, newspapers,
radio and TV broadcasters, 15 billion for

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:31.420
performance venues and independent movie theaters,
which are essentially shut down in total,

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:37.520
saves some rare examples that have figured
out how to do sort of like mask required.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.320
Everybody gets tested on the way in types
of things. There will be money for testing

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:48.100
and tracing 82 billion dollars for colleges
and schools, which many people have an issue

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:54.280
with the idea of some of these largely well-endowed
schools getting money when they don't even

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.439
really need to be charging tuition. They could
pay for everybody's tuition with the interest

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:03.640
on their endowments. That's a problem for
some 13 billion dollars for nutritional assistance,

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:09.910
seven billion for broadband access, 25 billion
for rental assistance and an extended eviction

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:14.910
moratorium. So basically, it's too little,
too late. And the devil is in the details

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:20.190
with a lot of these line items, for example,
just to pick one seven billion dollars for

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:24.440
broadband support.
How exactly does that work? Is it just a cash

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:31.860
grab for ISPs or is it actually reimbursements
for people who sign up for Internet service?

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:36.620
How is that that it's all in in the details?
Because these programs can either be beneficial

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:41.640
or slush funds for big corporations or both.
Admittedly, it can be it can be both. Now,

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.920
is it better than nothing? Well, yeah, of
course. Of course. With the caveat that sometimes

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:52.800
doing something crappy is used as an excuse
to not do anything else. So if I have a gunshot

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.500
wound and you hand me a Band-Aid, is the Band-Aid
better than nothing if more help is coming?

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.450
Well, yeah, it might be the Band-Aid might
do something for me for two minutes until

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:08.670
we get real treatment. But if handing me the
Band-Aid is all we do, well, then I'm going

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:14.840
to be screwed. And it's been seven months
since the last stimulus package. People are

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:21.290
getting half the cash payment and half the
enhanced unemployment. And now I I've been

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:26.650
getting voicemail's over the weekend from
people who seem to think the reason I did

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.940
a segment last week advocating for more. There's
people who seem to think I'm advocating for

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:36.820
more so that I will get more of something
I I don't even know that I need to do this.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:42.650
But I will mention that I am getting nothing.
I got nothing last time and neither did my

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:47.080
business. I'm getting nothing this time and
neither is my business. I'm not arguing for

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:53.410
even a single dollar for myself. I'm getting
zero either way. So it's half the benefits

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:59.860
for people as as the first time, half the
money is the first time and then the unemployment

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:05.650
benefits are half as big and they last for
only 11 weeks, about three months. So this

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:13.400
all counts on a dramatically strong recovery
that will be in full swing by March. And things

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:19.060
should be better by then as it starts getting
warmer again and people start being vaccinated

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:24.290
at a higher rate. But expecting anything approaching
a full recovery by three months from now seems

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:29.520
very silly. Some industries won't be fully
recovered for years. It is believed a huge

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:33.880
portion of small businesses are never reopening.
People are making zero right now. So much

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:40.561
like I said before, this was put together,
you know, if you're really struggling, six

00:04:40.561 --> 00:04:43.990
hundred dollars isn't going to do much for
you at all. It's been seven months. You get

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:48.720
600 bucks. It's not enough for a month's rent
in almost any part of the country. The unemployment

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:53.510
payments won't be retroactive. So if you've
been out of a job for the last several months,

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:58.690
that that's just gone too bad it's not retroactive.
And there are some on the right who are saying.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.031
You should be grateful that you got anything
the government doesn't owe you anything. Six

00:05:02.031 --> 00:05:07.480
hundred dollars is 600 more than the government
owes you. Well, the idea of owing is sort

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:13.030
of strange, but consider that the government
